---
layout: base.njk
title: Research
---
<section class="py-16">
  <div class="max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl tracking-tight mb-6 uppercase font-bold text-white" style="letter-spacing: 0.1em;">Research</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-6">I build computational models of human practices — a jazz performance, a union contract, a colonial book register — and then study what the model does to the practice, and whom the resulting system serves.</p>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 mb-4">The instruments are ordinary analytical ones: extraction pipelines, retrieval systems, real-time sensing, formal validation. The questions come from critical theory. Between them sits the thing I actually want to know:</p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[var(--color-secondary)] pl-6 my-10 text-xl text-white">When does formalising a practice make it contestable, and when does it quietly replace argument with a score?</blockquote>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400">That question has a test attached, and the test is what keeps this from being a mood. At any decision point, can the affected party raise an objection that the deciding party is obliged to answer in reasons — reasons of a kind they can dispute? A citation to a contract clause passes. A number does not: a score offers appeal, which is procedure, not argument.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-20 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 p-2">
    {% for s in sites %}
    <div class="card static-rainbow bg-[var(--color-bg-card)] rounded-xl p-6 flex flex-col">
      <p class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider text-xs mb-2">{{ s.mode }}</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">{{ s.title }}</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">{{ s.line }}</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm italic mb-4">{{ s.question }}</p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-auto">{{ s.theory }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="mt-24 max-w-4xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-8 uppercase tracking-wide">Three commitments</h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-lg uppercase tracking-wide text-white mb-2">Preserve before you translate</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-400">You cannot argue about what a thing was after you have overwritten it. The Punjab pipeline keeps the page image, the catalogue's verbatim words and the normalised layer as three separate things. The mixed-reality music work exists as five repositories and a verified vendor archive before any of it is ported. Preservation is not nostalgia; it is what makes the later argument checkable.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-lg uppercase tracking-wide text-white mb-2">Name what you refuse</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-400">KARL's charter refuses employer dashboards, productivity scoring and retention by default — affordances its own architecture would otherwise make trivial. ICTUS treats refusal as a formal design category. A system defined only by what it enables has not been designed, only assembled.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-lg uppercase tracking-wide text-white mb-2">Build for the side that did not have the tool</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-400">A contract only management can parse. A pedagogy only conservatory access grants. A print register that recorded a population without being readable by it. In each case the asymmetry is informational, and in each case it is reversible by the same instrument that produced it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-24">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-8 uppercase tracking-wide">Case studies</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 p-2">
      {% for p in projects %}
        {% if p.id in ["punjab", "karl", "strike"] %}
        <a href="{{ p.href }}" class="card static-rainbow bg-[var(--color-bg-card)] rounded-xl flex flex-col group transition-transform duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
          <div class="p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 uppercase tracking-wide">{{ p.title }}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">{{ p.line }}</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
